    "teacher_markdown": "A successful response may include:\r\n- Describes an array method as a built-in command or tool used to work with arrays.\r\n- Explains that array methods can add, remove, or manipulate items in an array without rewriting it manually.\r\n- Gives examples of common array methods and what they do, such as:\r\n\t- pop() — removes the last item from a list\r\n\t- push() — adds an item to the end\r\n\t- shift() — removes the first item\r\n\t- unshift() — adds an item to the beginning\r\n- Demonstrates understanding with an example\r\n- Notes that these methods change how the array looks or behaves, and can help organize or update lists efficiently.\r\n- May include a visual or mental model (like boxes for list items being rearranged or changed)."
